From 756c9edac3d043373f83c0e8202d680ed44902f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:59:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] review: stop the probe sweep, make export batches verifiable
 (schema 6), pin the baseline

Reviewed by a second Claude on macOS; this commit is its work plus one maintainer
adjustment (KEEP_SNAPSHOTS 7 -> 14 so the full .db snapshot outlives the CSV batch
retention of 14 days; the snapshot is the backstop when a consumer misses batches).

Fixed in the patch set:
- onFetchRecordedData ran enqueueProbeDownloads() on every sync: 17 file ids through
  0x2C, including sleep_data.bin / sleep_state.bin / rrisqi_data.bin, and threw the
  payload away. Now behind RESEARCH_FILE_PROBES = false.
- the delta cursor advanced even when a table or the manifest failed, so later rows of
  that table were never exported. It only advances on a complete batch now, and
  failed_tables says what is missing.
- unique_keys was a hand-kept list with a wrong activity key. It is read from
  PRAGMA table_info (files[].table / primary_key / key_columns).
- retention dropped manifests after 7 while keeping every CSV forever. One rule now:
  manifest + CSV batches are kept for KEEP_BATCH_DAYS (14), stale .json.tmp too.
- copyRawBlobs hashed the file and then copied it a second time, so an append in
  between left a checksum the archived copy did not have. The bytes are read once and
  the manifest now reports raw_archive[] with name / sha256 / bytes / changed / complete.
- writeManifest wrote the final name directly, so a consumer could read half a JSON.
  It writes .json.tmp and renames.
- appendRriToFile read the TLV length as one byte (a 15+ record packet needs two) and
  dropped sqi == 0 beats, which breaks the beat sequence irreversibly.
- GBApplication started PeriodicSyncScheduler before prefs existed (interval fell back
  to 6 h on every start) and kept the preference listener only weakly reachable.
- saveSleepDump: empty dumps are not saved, identical dumps are not saved twice, at
  most KEEP_SLEEP_DUMPS stay on disk.
- busy watchdog counted minutes across different tasks and kept running after dispose().
- data_quality gaps no longer count rows that share a timestamp.
- decoders/analyse_rri.py sorted whole rows, reordering the beats inside a packet and
  corrupting RMSSD / pNN50 (56.2 -> 40.1 ms on synthetic data).

Not verified here: no APK was built on the reviewing machine (it has no Gadgetbridge
dependencies) and nothing ran on the watch. Maintainer side: the patched tree compiles
(BUILD_OK, assembleMainlineDebug) and patches/all-changes.patch applies to the baseline;
device checks are listed in docs/review-2026-11-14.md section 3 and are still pending.
